 "about": "What each buyer projected for its first years, from Appendix A of its change in effective control application (Table 2, staff; Table 3, revenue and expenses). Every figure was copied from the page named here and checked by eye on November 10, 2026. Pages are PDF page numbers. nurse_fte = director of nursing + RNs + LPNs + nursing aides (and nursing administrators or medication aides when the table lists them); rn_fte = director of nursing + RNs (+ an RN nursing administrator). revenue = net patient revenue. profit = operating profit or loss. rent = the Leasehold Expenses or rent line, left out when the application labels it as mortgage, taxes, or property costs. mgmt = management or consulting fees, given only when the line is fees alone. staffing_ok false means the table's own payroll does not fit its staff counts, so the counts are not compared. Edit here to correct a figure; the page rebuilds from this file. cost_cap is the condition of approval in the adopted Health Services Council report that limits operating costs in the first full operating year; it is compared with the operating expenses on the cost report for the first whole year the buyer ran the home. past is the application's own nurse staff count for a year when the seller ran the home (on the page before the projections); the build compares it with the payroll records for that year, and if the two differ by more than 20% (payroll below 80% or above 125% of it) the application's staff counts are not compared, because they are not measuring the same thing.",
